---
rhumb: 0.1
title: Portolan
---

%% Portolan: a shared map of work for humans and AI agents. Rhumb is the plain-text language the map is written in.
%% Each node says what a piece of work is for; how it was built, with commands and numbers, is in the changelog behind the links.

- [/] Portolan ^portolan
  - Why: agents do long, branching work that logs and linear chat cannot show; people need one map of what is done, blocked and next.
  - [x] Prior-art survey {tags: [research]} ^survey
    - Why: before building anything, find out whether an open-source project already offers a shared mind map with tasks, comments and diary links.
    - Nothing covers it all; a few projects each cover one piece, so Portolan assembles its own.
    - [survey](../changelog.md#no-single-project-covers-the-whole-scope-closest-pieces-are-beadsbacklogmd-agent-task-graph-plannotator-annotateagent-feedback-simple-mind-mapmind-elixirmarkmap-mind-map-ui-tldraw-agent-kit-canvasagent-chat)
  - [x] Backlog.md analysis {tags: [research]} ^backlog-analysis
    - Why: Backlog.md came closest to keeping work as Markdown next to a diary, so its design deserved a closer look.
    - Its idea of human checkpoints is worth borrowing; its one-file-per-task format does not fit a daily diary.
    - [analysis](../changelog.md#yes-one-task-per-file-with-yaml-front-matter--fixed--sections-wrapped-in-html-comment-markers-cli-is-the-canonical-writer-hand-edits-discouraged)
  - [x] Naming: Portolan + Rhumb {kind: decision} ^naming
    - Why: a portolan chart was drawn from sailors' logbooks, with rhumb lines between ports: a map grown from logs.
    - The plain names were taken on npm, so the package is published under the author's scope.
    - [naming](../changelog.md#tentatively-named-portolan-project--rhumb-graph-dsl-rhumb)
  - [/] Rhumb DSL ^rhumb
    - Why: existing diagram languages have no notion of task status, dependencies or links into a diary, so the map needs its own language.
    - [x] Design decisions {kind: decision} ^rhumb-decisions
      - Why: agents write most of the map, so the language should reuse notations they already know and keep every item's identity stable.
      - Every item gets a short readable ID; links into the diary are written in the map, not in the diary.
      - [decisions](../changelog.md#rhumb-01-spec-written-peggy-based-parser-passes-17-tests-committed-as-portolan-ebeb107)
    - [x] Spec 0.1 {kind: artifact} ^rhumb-spec
      - Why: tools, tests and agents all need the same source of truth for what a map may contain.
      - [specification](../rhumb-spec.md)
    - [x] Test cases ^rhumb-tests
      - Why: the user asked for examples written as tests, so every rule is checked and changes cannot quietly break old maps.
      - [test approach](../changelog.md#rhumb-01-spec-written-peggy-based-parser-passes-17-tests-committed-as-portolan-ebeb107)
    - [x] Parser {tags: [peggy, typescript]} ^rhumb-parser
      - Why: checking, editing and the web view all start from the same understanding of a map.
      - [parser record](../changelog.md#rhumb-01-spec-written-peggy-based-parser-passes-17-tests-committed-as-portolan-ebeb107)
    - [/] Formatter ^rhumb-fmt
      - Why: people may leave out IDs or type status marks loosely; links and comments need stable IDs, so a formatter fills them in.
      - Missing IDs and loose status marks are fixed today; full layout tidying is still open.
      - [formatter scope](../changelog.md#edit-api-derive-anchor-resolver-threads-store-local-server-and-cli-landed-as-portolan-5a0a5d5-agent-guide-and-readme-written-by-subagents)
    - [x] Edit operations {tags: [agents]} ^rhumb-edit
      - Why: people, agents and the web view all edit the same file, and each change should stay a small, reviewable diff.
      - Every writer goes through the same operations, which refuse an edit that would break the map.
      - [edit operations](../changelog.md#edit-api-derive-anchor-resolver-threads-store-local-server-and-cli-landed-as-portolan-5a0a5d5-agent-guide-and-readme-written-by-subagents)
    - [x] Checker ^rhumb-check
      - Why: agents run the checker after each change, so broken structure, inconsistent status and dead diary links show up at once.
      - [x] Progress and readiness ^rhumb-derive
        - Why: progress and readiness are calculated when reading, never stored, so the file only holds the structure people write.
      - [x] Link resolver {tags: [links]} ^rhumb-resolve
        - Why: details live in the diary, so a link must land on the right entry, not just the right day.
    - [x] Expressiveness review {kind: finding, partial: true, tags: [research]} ^rhumb-review
      - Why: an experiment map needed to show controls, shared inputs and hypotheses, which raised whether the language was enough.
      - Hierarchy, status and the five kinds of relation cover most work; experiments stretched them.
      - [review](../changelog.md#keep-the-current-task-graph-foundation-prioritize-cross-file-references-and-a-small-set-of-semantic-node-and-relation-types-as-real-usage-exposes-gaps)
    - [x] Relation labels {kind: decision} ^rhumb-labels
      - Why: relations such as "compared against" only appear in some kinds of work, so they are written as short descriptions rather than new keywords.
      - "Needs" now only means "must happen first".
      - [relation labels](../changelog.md#keep-the-five-general-edge-kinds-domain-relations-are-verb-phrase-labels-on-a-directed-relates-portolan-7a2ade5)
    - [x] Line anchors {tags: [links]} ^rhumb-line-anchors
      - Why: a reader should land on the sentence or code that backs a claim, not on a whole day's notes.
      - Links can pick a line by how it starts, a few lines below it, or a line number; every link that misses is reported.
      - A text link without a heading searches the whole file; the guide says when to use which form.
      - [line anchors](../changelog.md#fragments-narrow-left-to-right-heading--line-prefix-l-l-offset-or-absolute-l42l42-l50-failures-are-w003-portolan-81619b4)
    - [x] Star marks ^rhumb-star
      - Why: people want to flag the items that matter most, and the whole project, agents included, should see the same stars.
      - Stars live in the map like any other property; agents add or remove them only when asked.
      - [star syntax](../changelog.md#shared-reserved-attribute-star-true-a-general-set-attr-edit-op-and-a-dedicated-star-ui-portolan-e39fff9)
    - [x] Node kinds ^rhumb-kinds
      - Why: experiment maps mix tasks with claims, and tools cannot tell them apart from free text.
      - Finishing an investigation must not read as proving its hypothesis; that rule comes before any fixed list of kinds.
      - Eleven preset kinds have their own icons; any other kind shows its shortest distinct letters in the map.
      - A claim's verdict is a flag such as `{refuted: true}`, kept apart from the item's status; at most one verdict holds.
      - [icon design](../changelog.md#11-preset-kinds-and-8-claim-icons-on-the-16-px-toolbar-grid-claim-states-became-boolean-attributes-like-star); [implementation](../changelog.md#kind--and-claim-flags-in-the-parser-spec-cards-legend-and-search-portolan-976233a)
    - [x] Doing and isolated checks {tags: [time]} ^rhumb-liveness
      - Why: a status that no longer matches the work below it, and an item no relation reaches, are both easy to miss by reading.
      - A doing group with nothing doing below it is `W018`; an isolated node among siblings is `I006`.
      - [the two checks](../changelog.md#w018-for-a-doing-group-with-nothing-doing-below-it-i006-for-an-isolated-node-portolan-49816fa)
    - [x] Timing {tags: [time]} ^rhumb-timing
      - Why: agents work for hours on one item, and people want to see whether it is on track without asking.
      - An item can carry an estimate, when its current run started and when it finished; these are rough working figures.
      - [timing attributes](../changelog.md#estimate-2h-started-2026-10-15t09300800-doing-cards-show-elapsed-against-estimate-green--amber-from-80--red-over); [finished and check report](../changelog.md#finished-and-actual-times-years-in-durations-a-timing-report-from-check-real-mission-times-in-the-demo-portolan-5ac7e78)
    - [?] Cross-map references {tags: [links]} ^rhumb-xref
      - Why: training, data and evaluation maps should share one model or dataset item instead of copying it.
      - Waiting until a second map really shares items with this one.
  - [?] Annotations and threads ^threads
    - Why: people want to comment on an item and talk with the agent there, on the map itself rather than in a separate review.
    - Conversations are kept next to the map, never inside it, so the map stays readable.
    - [x] Thread model ^threads-model
      - Why: flat comment lists lose context; each conversation should belong to one item and take part from both people and agents.
    - [x] Thread storage ^threads-format
      - Why: discussion must not clutter the map or its history, and several writers should not trip over each other.
      - [storage design](../changelog.md#edit-api-derive-anchor-resolver-threads-store-local-server-and-cli-landed-as-portolan-5a0a5d5-agent-guide-and-readme-written-by-subagents)
    - [/] Thread lifecycle ^threads-lifecycle
      - Why: renaming or deleting an item must not silently cut its conversations loose.
      - Renamed items keep their threads; threads of deleted items are flagged, but the checker does not look at them yet.
    - [x] Thread store ^threads-store
      - Why: the server, the comment view and the agent should all read and write the same conversations.
      - There is no command-line way to comment yet.
    - [ ] Agent loop {tags: [agents]} ^threads-agent
      - Why: talking with the agent in a comment only works if a person's comment reaches the agent and the reply comes back.
      - Open: how the agent learns about new comments.
    - [?] Comments on edges and links ^threads-targets
    - [?] Mentions and assignment ^threads-mentions
  - [x] Local server ^server
    - Why: one local process serves every map in a folder and applies changes from people and agents without one overwriting another.
    - It only accepts connections from this machine, because it has no login.
    - [edit API and server](../changelog.md#edit-api-derive-anchor-resolver-threads-store-local-server-and-cli-landed-as-portolan-5a0a5d5-agent-guide-and-readme-written-by-subagents)
  - [ ] Web view ^ui
    - Why: the user asked for a visual, interactive page that shows relations, progress and plans across the agent's work.
    - [x] Renderer choice {kind: decision} ^ui-spike
      - Why: the view must draw nested items and the relations between them, so the toolkit had to handle both.
      - [renderer choice](../changelog.md#react--vite--xyflow-map-view-with-status-editing-and-a-diary-panel-directory-mode-server-portolan-d2ce447)
    - [x] Map index ^ui-index
      - Why: serving a folder should show all its maps with their progress at a glance.
      - [index page](../changelog.md#react--vite--xyflow-map-view-with-status-editing-and-a-diary-panel-directory-mode-server-portolan-d2ce447)
      - The start page says in one line what Portolan is; it and the top bar link to the code on GitHub.
      - [GitHub links](../changelog.md#github-mark-at-the-right-end-of-the-top-bar-and-a-one-line-intro-under-the-map-index-portolan-caab2ea-49b96ed)
    - [x] Mind map view ^ui-tree
      - Why: the first view the user chose: status, progress and relations, so done, blocked and next work stand out.
      - Branches with no work in progress start folded; the card layout was later replaced by nested frames.
      - [web map view](../changelog.md#react--vite--xyflow-map-view-with-status-editing-and-a-diary-panel-directory-mode-server-portolan-d2ce447); [view tweaks](../changelog.md#status-tinted-cards-default-collapse--suffix-ids-portolan-fb6b7b6)
      - Pointing at a card shows its whole title without moving or resizing the card.
      - Only branches with work in progress open by default; starred items no longer keep a branch open.
      - [default folding](../changelog.md#history-life-primates-needs-history-life-neocortex-stars-no-longer-keep-a-branch-open-portolan-5e0aa8b-869c143)
    - [x] Folds stay put ^ui-fold-follow
      - Why: folding or unfolding relays the map out, and the card just clicked could jump away or out of sight.
      - Folding or unfolding an item pans the view so it stays where it was on screen.
      - [folds stay put](../changelog.md#the-view-is-panned-by-however-far-the-nodes-box-moved-in-the-relayout-then-nudged-inside-the-pane-portolan-94a2f5e)
    - [x] Hover focus {tags: [lines]} ^ui-hover
      - Why: with every relation drawn at once, lines and their text piled up; pointing at an item should pick out just its connections.
      - [hover focus](../changelog.md#hover-focus-portolan-c3c86c2-10-08-evening-then-nested-containers-laid-out-by-elk-3b74937)
      - Lines are always drawn; pointing at a line or an item highlights it, pointing at a label only shows its full text.
      - [always-visible lines and steady hover](../changelog.md#lines-above-frames-labels-above-all-full-text-on-hover-stable-hover-portolan-0a05378-64ad5e9)
      - Highlighting and labels fade in and out instead of switching at once.
      - [smooth transitions](../changelog.md#dimming-line-width-and-labels-now-ease-over-05-s-portolan-1d2ede6)
      - Highlighted cards lift with a soft shadow, the hovered one most.
      - [hover shadow](../changelog.md#the-hovered-card-lifts-with-a-drop-shadow-the-cards-its-highlight-reaches-with-a-lighter-one-portolan-c6c110f)
    - [x] Timeline layout {tags: [lines, time]} ^ui-layout
      - Why: the view was crowded and its reading order arbitrary; it should read like a timeline that respects what depends on what.
      - Groups are drawn as frames around their items, and lines are routed around cards.
      - Two groups that depend on each other cannot both sit above the other; a few lines there still point upward.
      - [container layout](../changelog.md#hover-focus-portolan-c3c86c2-10-08-evening-then-nested-containers-laid-out-by-elk-3b74937); [vertical order](../changelog.md#top-to-bottom-layout-prerequisites-above-dependents-siblings-stack-done-work-by-day-then-doing-todo-ideas)
      - Lines pass behind titles and controls unless highlighted; a small bar marks where each line leaves an item.
      - [lines behind titles, attachment tabs](../changelog.md#frames-are-split-into-a-fill-layer-below-the-lines-and-a-header-layer-above-them-portolan-faa0eaa)
      - A group sits where most of its finished and current work happened, so a few new ideas do not pull it down.
      - [group placement](../changelog.md#groups-are-placed-by-the-weighted-mean-of-their-leaves-times-donedoing-10-others-1-portolan-64d40b7)
    - [x] Readable labels {tags: [lines]} ^ui-labels
      - Why: labels on parallel lines covered each other, and later lines were drawn across them.
      - [label overlap](../changelog.md#labels-are-placed-along-their-own-edge-and-drawn-in-an-html-layer-above-all-edges-portolan-1089f0f)
      - Labels sit in front of everything and show their full text when their line is in focus or under the pointer.
      - Labels that would collide move up or down, never sideways, so each stays on its own line.
      - [label placement](../changelog.md#labels-now-stay-centred-on-their-own-line-and-move-only-up-or-down-portolan-08efdc9)
      - With all labels on, every line shows its label; a reason shared by several targets of one edge line appears once.
      - [missing needs labels](../changelog.md#label-dedupe-treated-every-unlabeled-edges-needs-as-a-repeat-portolan-95386d4)
    - [x] Star UI ^ui-star
      - Why: a star is only useful if starred items stand out and can be reached from anywhere.
      - Starred items are framed in gold, listed in a menu, and linked from the start page; a folded group shows how many it holds.
      - [star UI](../changelog.md#shared-reserved-attribute-star-true-a-general-set-attr-edit-op-and-a-dedicated-star-ui-portolan-e39fff9)
    - [x] Status editing ^ui-edit
      - Why: people should update progress where they read it, through the same path agents use, without overwriting someone else's change.
    - [x] Diary panel {tags: [links]} ^ui-diary
      - Why: the map only links to details, so the view shows the linked entry next to the selected item.
      - Editing only the diary does not refresh an open entry yet.
    - [x] Hot reload ^hot-reload
      - Why: agents and editors rewrite maps while a page is open; the view must stay current or people act on stale plans.
      - [hot reload](../changelog.md#per-directory-watchers-plus-a-2-s-rescan-recreated-files-no-longer-go-silent-portolan-05b336e)
      - Lines stay on screen while the map reloads; they used to blink out for a moment.
      - [lines blinking on reload](../changelog.md#every-line-blinked-out-for-about-200-ms-twice-per-reload-nodes-now-carry-their-measured-size-portolan-ad106cf)
    - [x] Connection status ^ui-connection
      - Why: when the server stopped, the page still looked live while edits failed and changes on disk stopped arriving.
      - An icon at the control bar's right end shows whether the live link to the server is up, says so in words when it is lost, and tests it on a click.
      - [silent drops](../changelog.md#it-did-not-the-page-looked-live-while-edits-failed-checked-by-killing-a-scratch-server-under-an-open-page); [connection status](../changelog.md#one-shared-event-stream-with-a-status-and-an-icon-that-tests-it-on-a-click-portolan-0192cb4)
    - [x] Warnings as an icon ^ui-warnings
      - Why: messages written onto the control bar pushed the controls about.
      - A failed reload, edit or layout shows as a warning triangle whose tooltip carries the message.
      - [warnings as an icon](../changelog.md#a-failed-reload-edit-or-layout-is-now-one-amber-warning-triangle-its-text-in-the-tooltip-portolan-75ba5b8)
    - [x] Freshness view {tags: [time]} ^ui-freshness
      - Why: on a large map, people need to spot active and neglected areas without reading dates.
      - A card's left edge is brighter the more recently its line or its dated diary entry changed.
      - [freshness](../changelog.md#freshness-view-from-git-blame-dated-links-and-child-nodes-portolan-7981b47-4a5bdc1)
      - Links into a changelog take the date of the dated section they land in.
      - [heading dates](../changelog.md#links-without-a-path-date-take-the-date-of-the-nearest-dated-heading-above-their-target-portolan-dcdae36)
      - Deep-past dates can be written in the Holocene calendar; anything older than a browser can show reads "long time ago".
      - [Holocene dates](../changelog.md#no-bce-before-headings-may-now-start-with--mm-dd-he-and-dates-beyond-the-js-range-show-long-time-ago-portolan-caae1df)
      - A map of past events can take its times only from its links (`dates: links`), so commit times do not override them.
      - [dates from links](../changelog.md#front-matter-dates-links-items-take-only-their-links-dates-and-git-is-not-read-on-in-the-civilization-demo-portolan-afbe2ee)
    - [x] Recent maps ^ui-recent
      - Why: switching maps meant going back to the start page every time.
      - [recent maps](../changelog.md#recent-maps-menu-and-click-to-copy-ids-and-commit-hashes-portolan-9dad94b)
    - [x] Copy IDs ^ui-copy
      - Why: IDs are what relations and shared links refer to, so copying one should not need careful selecting.
      - [copy IDs](../changelog.md#recent-maps-menu-and-click-to-copy-ids-and-commit-hashes-portolan-9dad94b)
    - [x] Legend and toolbar ^ui-legend
      - Why: colors, dash patterns and the bright left edge only help if a newcomer can look up what they mean.
      - View controls are compact icon buttons that name themselves on hover.
      - [legend and icons](../changelog.md#legend-popover-and-an-icon-toolbar-with-tooltips-portolan-f446de3)
      - A Source link in the bar opens the map's plain text in a new tab.
      - [source link](../changelog.md#source-portolanrhumb-opens-the-raw-rhumb-as-text-in-a-new-tab-portolan-93ea6e1)
      - The legend also explains kind icons, claim icons and the map's custom kind letters.
    - [x] Node search ^ui-search
      - Why: on a large map people look for an item by name or ID rather than scanning frames.
      - An exact ID jumps to its item; otherwise every match is outlined and the best ten are listed under the box.
      - [node search](../changelog.md#search-box-with-a-ranked-candidate-list-matches-are-outlined-on-the-map-portolan-b8f68ba)
      - `kind:hypothesis` and `is:refuted` narrow the search to one kind or claim state.
    - [x] History rail {tags: [time]} ^ui-history
      - Why: people want to see when a map changed and which items each change touched, without leaving the view.
      - Beside Diagnostics, each commit is a dot with its age; pointing at one highlights the items it changed. A map without commits shows its linked dates.
      - Clicking a point frames the items it changed, with the zoom capped so one small item does not fill the view.
      - [frame on click](../changelog.md#clicking-a-rail-dot-opens-the-groups-above-the-changed-nodes-and-fits-the-view-to-their-box-zoom-capped-at-about-11-portolan-f731362)
      - [history rail](../changelog.md#an-88-px-rail-at-the-far-right-next-to-diagnostics-commits-from-the-server-nodes-highlighted-on-hover-portolan-2513c2b)
      - Pointing at a commit opens its diff under Diagnostics, colored like a diff, until another dot or Close.
      - [diff panel](../changelog.md#diff-panel-under-diagnostics-pinned-to-the-last-hovered-point-diffs-computed-by-the-server-from-the-revision-texts-portolan-c2318bf)
    - [x] Timers {tags: [time]} ^ui-timers
      - Why: work in progress should show at a glance whether it is on time, nearly due or over.
      - Doing cards show the time since the start against the estimate, finished ones the time they took; Diagnostics lists timed work, most urgent first.
      - [timer chips](../changelog.md#estimate-2h-started-2026-10-15t09300800-doing-cards-show-elapsed-against-estimate-green--amber-from-80--red-over); [in-progress list](../changelog.md#an-in-progress-list-under-the-panels-dates-most-urgent-first-each-row-a-bar-of-elapsed-against-estimate)
      - A todo with an estimate shows what the work is expected to take before it starts.
      - [estimate on todos](../changelog.md#a-todo-with-an-estimate-and-no-start-shows-est-30y-as-a-grey-chip-portolan-faf49cd)
    - [x] Time-depth view {tags: [time]} ^ui-depth
      - Why: the map is laid out in time order already, but a flat plane cannot show how long a piece of work took or how far back an item's plan reaches.
      - A toolbar toggle gives the map time as a third dimension; the first cut lifted each item by its time over the flat map.
      - [time-depth view](../changelog.md#time-as-height-under-a-real-perspective-camera-the-gauge-on-the-ground-the-cards-floating-at-their-own-times-and-the-projection-done-in-points-so-pan-zoom-clicking-and-the-navigator-keep-working-portolan-1366444-b9fc359--the-perspective-rework)
      - [x] Panels on a level time axis {tags: [time]} ^ui-depth-panels
        - Why: lifted cards still faced the viewer square on, so the view did not read as 3D; each item has to stand in space at its own moment.
        - Time runs level through the map; each item is a perspective panel orthogonal to it, seen at 45°, and pointing at one shows its title flat.
        - [panels on a level axis](../changelog.md#time-runs-level-through-the-map-and-every-card-is-a-perspective-panel-at-its-own-moment-drawn-by-a-per-card-matrix3d-portolan-1609387)
      - [x] The navigator decides the 3D view {tags: [time]} ^ui-depth-pose
        - Why: the 3D view needs a fixed point of reference, and switching views should not lose one's place.
        - The navigator keeps the flat map; the items in its frame set the time axis's offset and length so they fill the screen, and switching is a camera move from the flat view.
        - [navigator decides the pose](../changelog.md#a-flat-navigator-a-pose-fitted-to-the-focus-nodes-and-a-camera-move-that-starts-on-the-flat-view-to-the-pixel)
      - [x] Timer bars {tags: [time]} ^ui-depth-bars
        - Why: how long work took or is taking is what a time axis is for.
        - Done items by their real start and finish, doing ones as a progress bar against the estimate, others by their estimate; bars that would cross are stacked.
        - [timer bars](../changelog.md#three-kinds-of-bar-by-status-stacked-into-lanes-where-they-cross-with-a-least-size-on-screen-portolan-0893051)
      - [x] Bars for folded work {tags: [time]} ^ui-depth-inferred
        - Why: a folded release with no times of its own showed nothing of how long it took.
        - A folded done item without times of its own takes its bar from the work inside it.
        - [inferred runs](../changelog.md#folded-done-nodes-take-their-run-from-the-earliest-start-to-the-latest-finish-inside-them-portolan-3c8722c)
    - [x] Compass-rose icon ^ui-favicon
      - Why: the app had no icon; a portolan compass rose ties the browser tab and the README to the project's name.
      - [favicon](../changelog.md#16-point-portolan-compass-rose-on-a-navy-tile-also-the-readme-logo-portolan-2dfaf35)
    - [x] Tab titles ^ui-tab-title
      - Why: with several maps open, every tab looked the same.
      - [tab title](../changelog.md#browser-tab-title-follows-the-map-title-portolan-57b3f25)
    - [ ] Annotation panel ^ui-threads
      - Why: people should annotate items and talk with the agent where they read the map; the first version left this out.
    - [?] Structural editing ^ui-struct-edit
      - Why: adding, removing or moving items and relations still means editing the text file; people should reshape the map where they read it, through the same edits agents use.
      - The edits behind it exist except moving a subtree; the first version left the controls out on purpose.
      - [first version scope](../changelog.md#react--vite--xyflow-map-view-with-status-editing-and-a-diary-panel-directory-mode-server-portolan-d2ce447)
    - [-] Dependency graph view ^ui-dag
      - Dropped: the timeline layout already shows what depends on what.
  - [x] Docs ^docs
    - Why: agents maintain the map themselves and need its rules; newcomers need to know why the project exists.
    - [README](../../README.md) explains the motivation; [skill.md](../skill.md) teaches agents to keep a map.
    - The guide asks for short plain titles and a "why" for every item, with technical detail kept in the diary.
    - [writing principle](../changelog.md#new-write-for-a-human-reading-the-big-picture-rule-in-skillmd-the-project-map-rewritten-by-it-portolan-2ad807f-diary-job-55234853)
    - The repository ships this map and a changelog copied from the diary, so readers there can follow every link.
    - [changelog and shipped map](../changelog.md#docschangelogmd-holds-the-35-portolan-diary-entries-docsportolanrhumb-is-now-the-project-map-linked-into-it)
    - The README example shows every kind of mark, and its image is drawn with the app's own icons.
    - [example marks](../changelog.md#the-readme-example-shows-7-preset-kinds-two-custom-ones-su-sp-every-verdict-style-and-two-qualifiers-same-commit-976233a)
  - [?] Agent interface {tags: [agents]} ^agent-api
    - Why: agents should read and change maps and comments through a proper tool interface, not only by editing text.
    - Command-line checks and the server exist; there are no agent tools yet.
  - [x] Publishing {kind: milestone} ^publish
    - Why: the code lived on one machine, and others can only use it once it is public and installable.
    - The code is public on GitHub; releases are set up to go to npm whenever the version number changes.
    - Released on npm (0.1.0, then 0.1.1 through the automatic workflow); the package carries its license and the bundled libraries' notices.
    - [npm scope and workflow](../changelog.md#package-k-l-lambdaportolan-builds-to-dist-publish-workflow-uses-npm-trusted-publishing-portolan-9957ecd)
    - The first manual release failed because the npm login on this machine had expired.
    - [publish error](../changelog.md#not-a-package-or-scope-problem-npm-did-not-recognize-the-login-both-available-tokens-return-401)
    - [license files](../changelog.md#license-bundled-third-party-notices-and-text-links-without-a-heading-portolan-65d90e1)
    - A read-only demo of this map runs on GitHub Pages and is rebuilt on every push.
    - [live demo](../changelog.md#read-only-demo-at-httpsk-l-lambdagithubioportolan-deployed-by-githubworkflowspagesyml-portolan-5eea371)
    - The demo now shows a folder of maps, including a fictional civilization-building map with deep-past dates and abandoned branches.
    - [demo folder](../changelog.md#the-project-map-is-now-docsdemoportolanrhumb-pages-exports-every-map-under-docsdemo-portolan-d59ccdd); [civilization branches](../changelog.md#15-branch-nodes-with-reasons-designer-voice-notes-for-the-life-stages-11-new-he-log-entries-committed-by-the-user-as-portolan-c8483af)
    - The civilization demo also shows kinds and claims; this map carries its own kinds and topic tags.
    - [demo claims](../changelog.md#12-kinds-and-every-claim-style-but-retracted-in-the-civilization-demo-portolan-c8fda73); [map kinds](../changelog.md#memoportolanrhumb-got-kinds-and-topic-tags-the-changelog-and-shipped-map-were-regenerated-from-the-diary-diary-job-7211fab1-portolan-ef29e2c)

%% Rhumb tooling
rhumb-spec needs rhumb-decisions
rhumb-tests needs rhumb-spec
rhumb-parser needs rhumb-tests
rhumb-fmt needs rhumb-parser
rhumb-edit needs rhumb-parser
rhumb-check needs rhumb-parser
rhumb-derive needs rhumb-parser
rhumb-resolve needs rhumb-parser
rhumb-line-anchors needs rhumb-resolve
rhumb-xref needs rhumb-check

%% Annotations
threads-format needs threads-model
threads-store needs threads-format
threads-lifecycle needs threads-store, rhumb-edit: renaming must carry its conversations along
threads-agent needs threads-store
threads-agent relates agent-api

%% Server, agents and UI
server needs rhumb-edit, rhumb-derive
agent-api needs rhumb-edit: agents change maps through the same safe operations
ui-spike needs rhumb-parser
ui-index needs server
ui-tree needs ui-spike, server
ui-edit needs ui-tree, rhumb-edit
ui-diary needs rhumb-resolve, server
hot-reload needs server
ui-freshness needs ui-tree, server
ui-hover needs ui-tree
ui-layout needs ui-tree, ui-freshness: items are ordered by when they changed
ui-labels needs ui-layout
ui-star needs rhumb-star, ui-edit
ui-search needs ui-tree
rhumb-liveness needs rhumb-derive, rhumb-check
rhumb-timing needs rhumb-parser
ui-timers needs ui-tree, rhumb-timing
ui-depth needs ui-timers, ui-history
ui-depth-pose needs ui-depth-panels
ui-depth-bars needs ui-depth-panels, ui-timers
ui-depth-inferred needs ui-depth-bars
ui-connection needs hot-reload
ui-warnings needs ui-edit
ui-fold-follow needs ui-tree
ui-history needs ui-freshness, ui-diary
ui-recent needs ui-index
ui-copy needs ui-diary
ui-legend needs ui-tree, ui-freshness
ui-threads needs threads-store, server
ui-struct-edit needs ui-edit
ui-dag needs ui-spike, server
ui-layout replaces ui-dag

